# Copy to .env at the repository root (git-ignored), then uncomment and fill in the lines you use.
# These are every variable the code reads; .env may also set others. A variable already set in
# the environment wins over this file.
# Every line is commented out because a blank KEY= sets "", which Harbor passes on as an empty
# credential instead of failing on the missing variable.
# Write one plain KEY=value per line, without `export` or inline comments: scripts/gateway.sh
# reads PORTKEY_API_KEY with grep, not python-dotenv.

## Credentials and endpoints

# Portkey gateway key: the route the runs (scripts/gateway.sh) and the labelers use by default.
# PORTKEY_API_KEY=
# Anthropic key, for Claude Code and OpenCode's Claude models without the gateway.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OpenAI key, for Codex and `ping-or-peek label --annotator openai` without the gateway.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# `ping-or-peek label`'s Portkey endpoint, if not https://api.portkey.ai/v1; `ping-or-peek code`
# always uses that default.
# PORTKEY_BASE_URL=
# The Anthropic endpoint the runs give Claude Code; scripts/gateway.sh sets it to Portkey's.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# Claude Code's extra request headers for Portkey; scripts/gateway.sh sets them from the key.
# PORTKEY_ANTHROPIC_HEADERS=

## Run settings (`ping-or-peek run`, `retry` and `confidentiality-test`)

# acpx build with caller input, for every harness but native Claude Code (README, "The forks").
# ACPX_PACKAGE=
# acpx build that passes Claude Code's thinking option, for native Claude Code jobs.
# CLAUDE_ACPX_PACKAGE=
# codex-acp build to use instead of the pinned release.
# CODEX_ACP_PACKAGE=
# Codex's container setting: seccomp-unconfined (the default) or privileged.
# CODEX_CONTAINER=
# Command that runs Harbor, if not the installed `harbor`, e.g. a patched build's binary.
# HARBOR=

## Private stores, outside the repository

# `ping-or-peek label`'s record store, when --label-root isn't given; it has no default.
# ASK_OR_SHORTCUT_LABEL_ROOT=
# `ping-or-peek code`'s private root for coded runs; it has no default.
# WS6_PRIVATE_ROOT=
